 of the 29 open matches</strong> carries a pick and a win probability, so this section has nothing to list. Nothing here is ever filled in with a default 50/50, and the limitations below are what would apply to any row a later refresh cannot price.</p><p class="small" data-ladder-counts="1"><strong>How each of the open matches got a pick, in the order it was tried:</strong> Polymarket exchange line, strict gate <strong data-ladder-count="exchange">14</strong> · HLTV fixture identity, rankings and lineups <strong data-ladder-count="hltv">0</strong> · Pinnacle esports moneyline <strong data-ladder-count="pinnacle">0</strong> · Wide exchange quote, labelled low confidence <strong data-ladder-count="exchange_wide">6</strong> · Researched bookmaker listing <strong data-ladder-count="book">3</strong> · Our own VRS model line <strong data-ladder-count="model_vrs">5</strong> · Our VRS model from HLTV’s dated Valve ranking <strong data-ladder-count="model_vrs_mirror">1</strong> · Research pick, no percentage <strong data-ladder-count="research">0</strong></p><p class="small">A match that no book or exchange prices is not dropped: it moves down the ladder to <a class="" href="https://www.hltv.org/matches">HLTV</a> for the exact fixture, ranking and lineup, then to a dated <a class="" href="https://egamersworld.com/counterstrike/matches">esportsbook listing</a>, and finally to <a class="" href="sources.html#model">our own Valve-standings model line</a>, which originates a percentage rather than quoting one. Only when every rung records a refusal or an absence does a row stay blank — <strong data-ladder-count="none">0</strong> at this snapshot. <a class="" href="unresolved.html">The full ladder, with the official source for each step →</a></p><ul class="checklist"><li><strong>A source that refuses or omits a price is a collection limit, not a finding.</strong> Access controls are never bypassed, a missing automated adapter is not evidence that a book has no line, and a blocked or unreadable page is recorded as such rather than converted into a number.</li><li><strong>Our own line needs both teams.</strong> The <a class="" href="sources.html#model">VRS model</a> prices a match only when both clubs resolve in Valve&rsquo;s official standings with a current roster; with one side missing the row drops to a research-only pick and no percentage is shown.</li><li><strong>Names and times must match exactly.</strong> A price moves between sites only for an exact team pair and UTC start, or through the <a class="" href="sources.html#method">verified alias register</a>. Where two sources disagree about the fixture itself the price is withheld and <a class="" href="review.html">flagged for review</a>.</li><li><strong>Evidence expires.</strong> Every percentage dies at the earliest of its eight-hour evidence window, the Hotspawn lock, the match start or the bookmaker cutoff, so a pick can vanish before a match starts if a refresh does not land.</li></ul><p class="glance-actions"><a class="button secondary" href="#unresolved-summary">Full unresolved section ↓</a><a class="button secondary" href="unresolved.html">Open the unresolved page →</a><a class="button secondary" href="review.html">Flagged for review →</a></p></section><section class="panel" id="unresolved-picks" aria-label="Unresolved picks and their limitations"><p class="eyebrow muted">Executive summary · unresolved picks &amp; limitations</p><h2>Picks without a win probability — and exactly why</h2><p><span data-count="missing">0</span> of the <span data-count="open">29</span> open matches publish no win percentage; <span data-count="unresolved">0</span> of those have no supported pick. Blank means unverified, never 50/50. Each row below states the source that was tried and the gate it failed.</p><p class="notice info"><strong>Nothing is blank.</strong> Every open match at this snapshot has a pick and a win probability.</p><details class="method-details"><summary>Evidence ladder &amp; source rules</summary><h3>What is tried, in order, before a blank is published</h3><p class="small">This is the publication ladder from <a class="" href="sources.html#method">the method page</a>. Hotspawn supplies the fixture list only; its crowd percentages are never used as a probability.</p><ol class="checklist ladder"><li><strong>1. Polymarket exchange line, strict gate</strong><p class="muted">Two-sided, funded and fresh: spread 25 points or less, at least $100 of liquidity, and an observation no older than eight hours. De-vigged from both outcome prices.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://gamma-api.polymarket.com/events">Polymarket Gamma API ↗</a></p></li><li><strong>2. HLTV fixture identity, rankings and lineups</strong><p class="muted">Confirms the exact opponent pair and UTC start, the world ranking and the current five. HLTV’s own betting table exposes no numeric two-way price to this collector, and its community vote is never used as a probability.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://www.hltv.org/matches">HLTV match pages ↗</a></p></li><li><strong>3. Pinnacle esports moneyline</strong><p class="muted">A sharp bookmaker’s two-way price for the exact fixture, de-vigged with the same formula. One bookmaker is not a consensus.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://guest.api.arcadia.pinnacle.com/0.1/sports/12/markets/straight">Pinnacle guest esports API ↗</a></p></li><li><strong>4. Wide exchange quote, labelled low confidence</strong><p class="muted">Used only when a row would otherwise have no pick at all: still two-sided, funding and freshness gates unchanged, spread between 25 and 60 points. The real spread is published.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://gamma-api.polymarket.com/events">Polymarket Gamma API ↗</a></p></li><li><strong>5. Researched bookmaker listing</strong><p class="muted">A dated two-way price read from a listing page, accepted only when it re-confirms the exact pair, the exact UTC start and an asymmetric pair bound to both team labels. The identical 1.8 / 1.8 placeholder some listings serve is refused, never published.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://egamersworld.com/counterstrike/matches">EGamersWorld CS2 listing ↗</a></p></li><li><strong>6. Our own VRS model line</strong><p class="muted">Valve’s official Regional Standings points through Valve’s own published expected-win formula and calibration. Labelled as our model everywhere; never presented as a market price.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://github.com/ValveSoftware/counter-strike_regional_standings">Valve counter-strike_regional_standings ↗</a></p></li><li><strong>7. Our VRS model from HLTV’s dated Valve ranking</strong><p class="muted">Only when Valve’s monthly file cannot resolve the clubs: the same formula and calibration, with points from HLTV’s dated Valve-points list, explicit provenance and the same expiry gates. Not an operator price or a claim that HLTV’s current points occur in the older monthly file.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://www.hltv.org/valve-ranking/teams">HLTV dated Valve ranking ↗</a></p></li><li><strong>8. Research pick, no percentage</strong><p class="muted">Ranking-order evidence for an exact fixture — or, when HLTV lists no fixture page, each club’s world rank on its own exact HLTV team page (an unranked side counts only where HLTV states the absence in words) — one side listed in Valve’s official standings while the other side is absent from that file, or — weakest and last — HLTV’s own recent completed results for both teams on the fixture page (more wins over the same number of recent matches; HLTV’s lifetime head-to-head series wins break a tie; still level stays unresolved). A directional pick only — the percentage and the fair odds stay blank.</p><p class="small">Source: <a class="" href="https://www.hltv.org/ranking/teams">HLTV rankings and Valve standings ↗</a></p></li></ol></details><p class="small"><a class="" href="unresolved.html">Full unresolved &amp; non-market queue →</a> · <a class="" href="unresolved.html#coverage-boundary">Matches that can never carry a pick →</a> · <a class="" href="sources.html">Source health and access results →</a> · <a class="" href="review.html">Flagged for review →</a></p></section><details class="briefing-more" id="detailed-summary"><summary>Detailed tables, source attempts &amp; coverage notes</summary><nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Where the picks are"><a href="picks.html">Updated picks (<span data-count="open">29</span>)</a><a href="unresolved.html?status=needs">No percentage (<span data-count="missing">0</span>)</a><a class="" href="matches.html">Every match (92)</a><a class="" href="analysis.html">TWC day 1–5 analysis</a><a class="" href="analysis.html#day-four-results">Day-4 results</a><a class="" href="analysis.html#day-three-results">Day-3 results (record)</a></nav><div class="notice info" id="coverage-line"><strong>Coverage at 24 Oct · 08:06 UTC:</strong> <span data-count="open">29</span> open fixture(s) — <span data-count="priced">29</span> with published probabilities (<span data-count="market">23</span> from markets, <span data-count="model">6</span> from our VRS model), <span data-count="researched">0</span> with a labelled research-only pick and no percentage, <span data-count="unresolved">0</span> with no supported pick yet. <a class="" href="picks.html">Open the pick board →</a> · <a class="" href="#unresolved-summary">Jump to the unresolved section ↓</a></div><section class="stats" aria-label="Coverage at last check" id="coverage"><a class="stat" href="matches.html?status=open"><div class="stat-label">Open matches <span>↗</span></div><strong data-count="open">29</strong><span class="stat-foot">92 total feed entries</span></a><a class="stat green" href="picks.html"><div class="stat-label">With probabilities <span>↗</span></div><strong data-count="priced">29</strong><span class="stat-foot"><span data-count="percent">100</span>% of open · 23 market · 6 model</span></a><a class="stat amber" href="unresolved.html"><div class="stat-label">No market line <span>↗</span></div><strong>06</strong><span class="stat-foot">6 model line(s) · 0 research pick(s) · 0 unresolved</span></a></section><section class="panel" id="phone-tips" aria-label="Refresh schedule and how to read a row"><p class="eyebrow muted">Refresh &amp; how to read a row</p><h2>Updated picks, on a schedule.</h2><p>The collector checks Hotspawn on a <strong>15-minute schedule</strong>, with a <strong>10-minute watchdog</strong> that requests a refresh when the published snapshot is over <strong>90 minutes old</strong>. GitHub may delay a run, so every row publishes its observation and expiry time. <strong data-count="missing">0</strong> currently open match(es) have no verified win percentage: choose <em>No percentage</em> on <a class="" href="unresolved.html?status=needs">Unresolved</a> to see the reason for each. Unsupported numbers stay blank.</p></section><div class="notice info"><strong>Our own lines fill the market gaps.</strong> <span data-count="model">6</span> open match(es) have no usable betting line, so the probability is <strong>our originated line</strong>: Valve’s official Regional Standings points run through Valve’s own published win-expectation formula and calibration. It is labelled on every row and never presented as a market price. <a class="" href="sources.html#model">How the model works and how it compares with the market →</a></div><div class="notice"><strong>Coverage is not the same as certainty.</strong> <span data-count="unresolved">0</span> open match(es) have no supported pick at all. Names can differ across providers, some markets lack usable prices, model inputs can be ambiguous, and HLTV or esportsbook access may be restricted. <a class="" href="unresolved.html">See every non-market and unresolved match →</a></div><div class="notice info" id="twc-unpriced"><strong>Unresolved picks &amp; their limitations:</strong> 0 research-only pick(s) carry no percentage, and 0 open row(s) have no supported pick; each one is listed in the unresolved section below with the gate it failed and the source it was sought from. The 3 dated final-day research limits remain on the analysis page as a completed-event record. <a class="" href="#unresolved-summary">Unresolved section ↓</a> · <a class="" href="analysis.html#day-five-guidance">Day-5 final-day guide (record) ↗</a> · <a class="" href="analysis.html#day-five-guidance-unpriced">Archived final-day limits ↗</a> · <a class="" href="unresolved.html">All non-market rows →</a></div><div class="section-heading" id="today"><div><p class="eyebrow muted">Executive summary · today</p><h2>Today\'s picks · 24 Oct · 08:06 UTC</h2><p>13 priced pick(s) start today, in start-time order: the team named in the pick box is the recommendation, and the percentage beside it is its market-implied or modelled chance. All times are UTC; a pick is withheld once its evidence or the Hotspawn lock passes.</p></div><a class="" href="picks.html">All updated picks →</a></div><details class="more board-more"><summary>Show the full table: 13 priced pick(s) starting today — every column, source link and calculation</summary><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Today&#x27;s picks"><table role="table"><caption>Whole-match winner only. Blank percentages = unverified; never a default 50/50. Times UTC.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Match / event</th><th scope="col">Start / lock</th><th scope="col">Win probability</th><th scope="col">Our pick</th><th scope="col">Sources</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="row" data-needs="0" data-match="1079659" data-status="priced" data-search="spirit academy lavked cct europe 2026 series #11 1079659" data-event="CCT Europe 2026 Series #11" data-start="2026-10-24T11:00:00Z" data-lock="2026-10-24T10:54:00Z" data-expires="2026-10-24T10:54:00Z" data-evidence="2026-10